map_prompt:
You answer a question about a text collection using ONLY the community reports below (each report summarises one topic area of a knowledge graph).
Return ONLY a JSON object: {"points": [{"description": str, "score": int}]} where each point is a partial answer in one or two sentences with a helpfulness score from 0 to 100 (how much that point helps to answer the question; 0 if irrelevant). Give at most 5 points. If nothing is relevant return {"points": [{"description": "nothing relevant", "score": 0}]}.

Question: {q}

Community reports:
{reports}

reduce_prompt:
You answer a question about a text collection by combining partial answers (points) produced from different parts of it. They are sorted by helpfulness score, highest first. Remove irrelevant and duplicate points, merge related ones, and write a final answer of at most 200 words in plain text. Use only the points. Name the techniques; do not invent facts.

Question: {q}

Points:
{pts}

report_prompt:
You write a short report on one community (cluster) of a knowledge graph built from Wikipedia articles on machine learning.
Use only the entities, relationships and passages given. Return ONLY a JSON object: {"title": str (short, names the main topic), "summary": str (3 to 5 sentences), "findings": [str, str, str] (3 key facts, one sentence each)}.

Entities (name, type):
{ents}

Relationships (source -relation-> target):
{rels}

Passages:
{pas}
